messages:
mira: opened PR to add a 'fallback_mode' column in the model catalog and a short SDK v4 snippet for per-request fallback control. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/10177

eli: nice. can you show the opt-out example? ops keeps asking for a canonical snippet to block fallback per request.

mira: sure, pasted in PR: 
```js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY });

await client.generate({
  model: 'zephyr-mini-4b@2026-12-01',
  input: 'Summarize the new catalog fields',
  routing: { allow_fallback: false }
});
```

sam: also add a small YAML example for model-card maintainers showing `seq_ceiling` and `fallback_mode: conditional`. keeps expectations clear.

mira: added YAML snippet and a one-line benchmark summary (public excerpt). noted internal CSV kept internal-only.

docs-bot: running link-check and snippet-lint on PR #10177. snippet-lint OK. external links OK. internal links flagged as internal-only.

eli: LGTM aside from tiny wording nit. I'll merge after docs-bot green.

mira: fixed wording, merging. follow-up: sweep model cards for missing `seq_ceiling` tags.

sam: I'll take the sweep. thanks.

mira: closing thread. if routing behavior questions pop up, ping #eng-runtime.
